<title>JAPAN: Yamaichi Sec shares ask-only after raid report.</title>
<headline>Yamaichi Sec shares ask-only after raid report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Yamaichi Securities Co Ltd were ask-only on the Tokyo Stock Exchange early on Wednesday morning after a media report that prosecutors began searching its headquarters over suspicions of its involvement in a &quot;sokaiya&quot; racketeer payoff scandal.</p>
<p>Yamaichi shares were ask only at 296 yen against Tuesday's close of 301.  </p>
<p>The Japanese business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said on Wednesday that Yamaichi provided 80 million yen to racketeer Ryuichi Koike, who is a key figure in a high-profile payoff scandal.</p>
<p>Yamaichi spokesmen were not immediately available for comment on the reports.</p>
